What is NAT?

Most devices are behind routers.

Example:

Laptop -> 192.168.1.10
Phone   -> 192.168.1.11
TV      -> 192.168.1.12

These private IP addresses are not directly accessible from the internet.

Routers use:

NAT (Network Address Translation)

NAT often prevents direct peer communication.

WebRTC solves this using:

STUN
TURN
ICE